{
  "id": "21332_youninsuru",
  "headword": "{容認|ようにん}する",
  "reading": "ようにんする",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb (transitive)",
  "gloss": "to tolerate; to accept; to approve",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to tolerate; to accept; to approve; to condone",
      "explanation": "To accept or allow something, often something that might otherwise be objectionable. Implies a deliberate decision to permit rather than enthusiastic endorsement."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21332_youninsuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{政府|せいふ}がそれを{容認|ようにん}した。",
      "english": "The government approved it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21332_youninsuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "このような{行為|こうい}は{容認|ようにん}できない。",
      "english": "Such conduct cannot be tolerated.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21332_youninsuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{国際|こくさい}{社会|しゃかい}は{核兵器|かくへいき}の{使用|しよう}を{容認|ようにん}すべきではない。",
      "english": "The international community should not condone the use of nuclear weapons.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {容|よう} (contain, tolerate) + {認|にん} (acknowledge). A formal word often used in political, legal, and diplomatic contexts. Implies accepting something as permissible rather than positively endorsing it.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {暗黙|あんもく}の{容認|ようにん}: tacit approval\n- {容認|ようにん}できない: unacceptable, intolerable\n- {容認|ようにん}{姿勢|しせい}: stance of acceptance\n- {容認|ようにん}{範囲|はんい}: acceptable range\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {許可|きょか}する: to permit (official authorization)\n- {承認|しょうにん}する: to approve (formal endorsement)\n- {黙認|もくにん}する: to tacitly approve (knowing but not objecting)\n- {認|みと}める: to acknowledge, to approve (broader, everyday usage)",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
